@startuml
title UC-06 - V03 Definition-selected internal workload
autonumber
actor Developer
control DeploymentService as Service
control PlanningService as Planner
control DefinitionMatcher as Matcher
control ResourceProvisioningService as Provisioner
boundary ExistingClusterAdapter as Cluster
control ConnectionCredentialResolver as Credentials
boundary TerraformExecutor as TF
control WorkloadRenderer as Renderer
boundary WorkloadDeployer as Workload
boundary ResourceCleanupService as Cleanup
database DeploymentRepository as Repo
Developer -> Service: Import Score / Preview / Deploy(app, env)
Service -> Planner: immutable scope/catalog/current/config snapshot
Planner -> Matcher: Select workload Definition/class first
Matcher --> Planner: lifecycle selection + refs/provision
Planner -> Planner: Expand references and provision to fixed point
Planner -> Matcher: Match namespace / cluster / companion Definitions
Matcher --> Planner: cluster Driver Account and resource pins
Planner -> Planner: Validate typed namespace/cluster agreement, DAG\nand one-cluster V03 capability; provider-first batches
Planner --> Service: Safe per-node placement and pinned plan
Service -> Renderer: Verify installed bundle/binary before effects
Service -> Repo: Admit owner/fence, versions, immutable plan
Service -> Provisioner: Execute resource-only batches
Provisioner -> Cluster: Resolve matched preexisting cluster
Cluster -> Credentials: Resolve pinned Internal account privately
Credentials --> Cluster: invocation-only credential
Cluster --> Provisioner: checked opaque typed cluster target
Provisioner -> TF: Provision owned namespace / companions on exact target
TF --> Provisioner: validated outputs / owned state
Provisioner --> Service: per-resource typed outputs/targets
Service -> Renderer: Render Score + resolved namespace/cluster/bindings
Renderer --> Service: validated internal manifests
Service -> Workload: Apply exact target and namespace
Service -> Workload: WaitReady exact workload identity
Workload --> Service: Ready or explicit failure
opt Resource depends on completed workload under provision flags
  Service -> Provisioner: Execute ready resource-only post-workload subset
  Provisioner --> Service: validated outputs / persisted progress
end
Service -> Repo: Commit current/instances/SUCCEEDED only after all required stages Ready
Developer -> Service: Update image/config; restart then operate
Service -> Repo: Restore original per-workload target/pins
Developer -> Service: Remove workload; explicitly confirm owned cleanup
Service -> Workload: Delete applied objects on persisted target
Service -> Cleanup: Destroy only confirmed owned namespace/resources
Cleanup --> Developer: absence verified; existing cluster retained
note over Developer, Repo
V03 real acceptance frontend only; backend/jobs/PostgreSQL/Redis deferred V04.
No fake dependency PASS. No Environment Connection selector after V03.10.
end note
@enduml
